r4-pro: add the pwm-fan the board actually has, with cooling maps.

BPI-R4Pro-V10 carries two populated 4-pin fan headers (CN36/CN38, "KK 254 PIN1R
FOR FAN": 12V, GND, PWM, TACH) driven from GPIO57_PWMD0 through R895 0R, and the
enclosure fan plugs into one of them. The DTS brought up in 990 declared no fan
and did not enable the PWM controller at all, so /sys/class/pwm was empty, no
cooling_device existed, and the thermal framework had no way to regulate that
fan -- it just ran at whatever the header defaults to. network.get_resources
correspondingly reported the board as fanless, which was accurate but only
because the software could not see the hardware.

Found during TEST-ACCEPTANCE §9.2 on r4-pro and confirmed against
BPI-R4Pro-V10-SCH-20250806 sheet CM19.

The drive is direct (0R series, no inverting stage), unlike r3/r3-mini whose
pwm-fans are inverted, so cooling-levels rise with duty. Channel, period and the
115/85/40C active trips mirror what OpenWrt already ships for the MT7988A r4
(patches-6.12/180), since it is the same SoC and the same PWM channel 0.

The headers also carry TACH. Wiring that up would make r4-pro the first board in
this product able to populate fan_rpm, but it needs the tach GPIO's interrupt
mapping; left for a follow-up rather than guessed at here.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-8x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-8x.dts
@@ -30,6 +30,18 @@
 		rootdisk-spim-nand = <&ubi_rootfs>;
 	};
 
+	fan: pwm-fan {
+		compatible = "pwm-fan";
+		/* CN36/CN38 are 4-pin KK254 fan headers (12V, GND, PWM, TACH) driven
+		 * from GPIO57_PWMD0 through R895 0R -- a direct, non-inverted drive,
+		 * so duty rises with cooling demand (BPI-R4Pro-V10 sheet CM19).
+		 * Same PWM channel and period the MT7988A r4 uses. */
+		cooling-levels = <0 80 128 255>;
+		#cooling-cells = <2>;
+		pwms = <&pwm 0 50000>;
+		status = "okay";
+	};
+
 	memory@40000000 {
 		reg = <0x00 0x40000000 0x00 0x10000000>;
 		device_type = "memory";
@@ -74,6 +86,51 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&pwm {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&cpu_thermal {
+	/* mt7988a.dtsi declares only the 125C critical trip; the active trips that
+	 * drive a fan live in the per-board dtsi, so mirror the MT7988A r4 ramp. */
+	trips {
+		cpu_trip_active_high: active-high {
+			temperature = <115000>;
+			hysteresis = <2000>;
+			type = "active";
+		};
+
+		cpu_trip_active_med: active-med {
+			temperature = <85000>;
+			hysteresis = <2000>;
+			type = "active";
+		};
+
+		cpu_trip_active_low: active-low {
+			temperature = <40000>;
+			hysteresis = <2000>;
+			type = "active";
+		};
+	};
+
+	cooling-maps {
+		map-cpu-active-high {
+			cooling-device = <&fan 3 3>;
+			trip = <&cpu_trip_active_high>;
+		};
+
+		map-cpu-active-med {
+			cooling-device = <&fan 2 2>;
+			trip = <&cpu_trip_active_med>;
+		};
+
+		map-cpu-active-low {
+			cooling-device = <&fan 1 1>;
+			trip = <&cpu_trip_active_low>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
 &eth {
 	status = "okay";
 };
